---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import DocsHandoff from '../components/DocsHandoff.astro';
import { askQuestionHref, describeServiceHref } from '../data/contact';

const pageTitle = 'FAQ | Registry Stack';
const pageDescription =
  'Answers for government teams about Registry Stack: service fit, control of records, starting configurations, implementation, costs and support.';

// Grouped so a reader can scan to their own concern. Each answer stays short and
// links to the page that carries the depth, so the FAQ does not become a second
// copy of the site.
const groups = [
  {
    "heading": "Fit for your service",
    "items": [
      {
        "q": "What does Registry Stack help us do?",
        "a": "You can build and adapt public registers and the services that use them. For example, a licensing authority can maintain licence records, assign renewal requests to officers and let another service check a licence's recorded status.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Explore the solution areas",
          "href": "/solutions/"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "Which products do we need?",
        "a": "Start by describing the service you need. Base Registry Engine maintains records. Registry Casework assigns requests to staff and records decisions. Evidence Gateway checks information from a register and gives another service the agreed answer. You can use one product or combine them with existing systems.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Compare the products",
          "href": "/solutions/#products"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "Is Registry Stack for national, regional or local government?",
        "a": "Registry Stack can support all three. A national regulator, regional administration or local authority can adapt the records, access rules and review steps to its responsibilities. Start with the service you need to improve, such as licensing, business registration or maintaining a health facility register.",
        "link": {
          "label": "See the solution areas",
          "href": "/solutions/"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "Who is behind Registry Stack?",
        "a": "Aubex Consulting LLC builds and supports Registry Stack and offers paid implementation and technical support. The company is based in San Francisco, United States.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Read the company details",
          "href": "/imprint/"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "Can we keep our existing register?",
        "a": "Yes, where your system can provide the required information. Evidence Gateway can let another service check a supplier's registration status, for example, while your register stays in its current system. The implementation team checks how to connect the systems. Your institution decides what another service may receive, and the team configures those rules.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Explore Evidence Gateway",
          "href": "/products/evidence-gateway/"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "What needs to be added to make a working service?",
        "a": "The core products handle records, staff reviews and information checks. Your service also needs user screens, sign-in, connections to other systems and arrangements for hosting and support. Your team or an implementation partner provides this work. A paid pilot can include the parts you agree with us.",
        "link": {
          "label": "See the implementation options",
          "href": "/pricing/"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "heading": "Your records and implementation",
    "items": [
      {
        "q": "Who controls our records?",
        "a": "Your institution sets the access rules: who may view, add or change records, and what other services may receive. You or a provider you appoint runs the software. The core software does not send your records or audit logs to Aubex.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Read about security and responsibilities",
          "href": "/security/"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "What will our team need to do?",
        "a": "Your institution defines the service rules, approves who may access or receive information, and names the people responsible for the service and its records. You also agree how to check that the service meets your requirements. The proposal assigns the remaining delivery and handover work to your team, our team or another provider.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Discuss implementation and support",
          "href": "/pricing/"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "Can we start from a spreadsheet or existing database?",
        "a": "Yes, with data preparation. Your team can prepare existing data for a new register or for specific information checks. The implementation must define how fields match, how errors are checked and how the data will be kept up to date. This work is agreed as part of the implementation.",
        "link": {
          "label": "See how we adapt a service",
          "href": "/customization/"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "Can one connection support more than one information check?",
        "a": "Yes, when the checks use the same source system and access arrangements. A connection to a company register could support checks of both registration status and registered address. Your institution still defines what each check may return and who may request it. Other sources may need separate connections.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Explore information checks",
          "href": "/solutions/check-a-fact/"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "How do we know whether information is up to date?",
        "a": "The time an answer was checked is different from the time the source record was updated. Your implementation needs rules for how recent the information must be, especially when using a copy of a register. A digital signature lets the receiving service check who issued the answer and whether it was altered; it does not prove that the source information is current or correct.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Read about information checks and dates",
          "href": "/solutions/check-a-fact/#faq"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "Can we issue verifiable credentials?",
        "a": "Yes. A professional council can issue a digitally signed statement of licence status. The professional receives it in a compatible digital wallet and presents it to an employer. The implementation connects and tests the wallet and the employer's receiving service. Issued credentials do not update with the register, and Registry Stack currently cannot cancel them before they expire.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Explore verifiable credentials",
          "href": "/solutions/verifiable-credentials/"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "heading": "Starting configurations",
    "items": [
      {
        "q": "What is a starting configuration?",
        "a": "A starting configuration, also called a starter, defines the records, permitted changes and access roles for one kind of register. Your team can adapt it to your institution's rules. It provides a starting point for a service; the screens, system connections and operating arrangements still need to be supplied.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Browse starting configurations",
          "href": "/starters/"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "How do we get a starting configuration?",
        "a": "Starting configurations are free on request. Use the request button on a catalogue page to name the configuration, or tell us what you need if you are unsure which one fits. We send the configuration for your team to evaluate and adapt.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Find a starting configuration",
          "href": "/starters/"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "Do we need to choose a configuration before contacting you?",
        "a": "No. Describe the service, who will use it and what you want to improve. Our team can help identify a suitable starting configuration and discuss the changes needed.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Describe the service you need",
          "href": describeServiceHref('a service that needs a starting configuration')
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "heading": "Costs, evaluation and support",
    "items": [
      {
        "q": "Is there a software licence fee?",
        "a": "Base Registry Engine, Evidence Gateway and Registry Casework are open source under Apache 2.0, with no software licence fee. Implementation and technical support are paid services. Separate products such as Registry Studio have their own terms.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Read the licensing summary",
          "href": "/terms/#terms-license-title"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "Do we have to buy support to use the software?",
        "a": "No. You can use the core software with your own team or a provider you choose. You are responsible for arranging hosting and maintenance, and the supplied licence and attribution requirements still apply.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Use Registry Stack with your own team",
          "href": "/pricing/#self-service"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "How mature is the software?",
        "a": "The core software is in Beta for institutional pilots. Your organization or a provider you appoint runs it. Expect changes as the software develops, and agree hosting, support and upgrade responsibilities for your pilot.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Read the known limitations",
          "href": "https://docs.registrystack.org/explanation/known-limitations/"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "How can our technical team evaluate it?",
        "a": "Start with the introductory tutorials. They cover creating a small register, setting permissions and trying an information check. Your team can then review the documentation and source code against your requirements. Setup and configuration instructions are in the documentation.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Choose an introductory tutorial",
          "href": "/#developers"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "What implementation and support services are available?",
        "a": "An implementation pilot helps your team configure, test and evaluate a defined service. The proposal states what is included and whether it covers a test service or a live deployment. Annual technical support is available for teams that implement and operate Registry Stack themselves. The work, responsibilities and fee are agreed in writing before starting.",
        "link": {
          "label": "See implementation and support pricing",
          "href": "/pricing/"
        }
      },
      {
        "q": "Can AI help customize our service?",
        "a": "Yes, through an implementation pilot with our team. We use AI tools to help adapt records, forms and review steps, then review and test the result with you. AI does not replace your institution's decisions, and the configured service does not need AI for ordinary operation. Registry Studio is in development; its self-service AI assistant is planned.",
        "link": {
          "label": "Explore AI-assisted customization",
          "href": "/customization/"
        }
      }
    ]
  }
];

// FAQPage structured data, built from every group's question and answer so the
// markup stays in step with the visible FAQ.
const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: groups.flatMap((group) =>
    group.items.map((item) => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: item.q,
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: item.a,
      },
    })),
  ),
};
---

<Base title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <SiteHeader current="faq" />

  <main>
    <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="faq-hero-title">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
          <h1 id="faq-hero-title">Frequently asked questions.</h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">
            Find out how Registry Stack can fit your service, who controls your
            records, and what implementation and support involve.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {groups.map((group, index) => (
      <section class={index % 2 === 1 ? 'section section-muted' : 'section'} aria-labelledby={`faq-group-${index}`}>
        <div class="section-inner">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <h2 id={`faq-group-${index}`}>{group.heading}</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-list">
            {group.items.map((item) => (
              <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>{item.q}</summary>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                  <p>{item.a}</p>
                  <a class="inline-cta" href={item.link.href}>{item.link.label} &rarr;</a>
                </div>
              </details>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    ))}
  </main>

  <DocsHandoff
    heading="Still have a question?"
    body="Tell us about the service you need and what you would like to know."
    primaryLabel="Ask a question"
    primaryHref={askQuestionHref()}
    emphasis="docs"
  />
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .faq-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: clamp(20px, 3vw, 28px);
    max-width: 820px;
  }

  .faq-item {
    background: var(--registry-white);
    border: 1px solid var(--registry-rule);
  }

  .faq-item summary {
    align-items: center;
    color: var(--registry-ink);
    cursor: pointer;
    display: flex;
    font-size: var(--type-body);
    font-weight: 700;
    gap: 16px;
    justify-content: space-between;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 18px 20px;
  }

  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  /* A register tick that opens into a cross, so the control reads without
     relying on a dash glyph. */
  .faq-item summary::after {
    color: var(--registry-blue);
    content: '+';
    font-family: var(--registry-mono);
    font-size: var(--type-subhead);
    line-height: 1;
    transition: transform 0.15s ease;
  }

  .faq-item[open] summary::after {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }

  .faq-item summary:hover {
    color: var(--registry-blue);
  }

  .faq-answer {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--registry-rule);
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 16px 20px 20px;
  }

  .faq-answer p {
    color: var(--registry-body);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .faq-item summary::after {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
